5.3 The BSC shall meet at least once per quarter. Additional meetings may be convened by the Chair as necessary. A quorum shall be half of the membership plus one. Decisions shall be taken by simple majority, and the Chair shall have a casting vote in the event of a tie.

5.4 The Office of Safety, Health and Environment (OSHE) shall:

a) Provide administrative support to the BSC, including the maintenance of the central register of approved projects, risk assessments, and training records;

b) Advise Principal Investigators and laboratory staff on the interpretation of this policy and on the selection of appropriate containment measures;

c) Coordinate the delivery of biosafety training and maintain records of training completion for all personnel who work with biological materials;

d) Conduct routine inspections of laboratories at least twice a year, and additional inspections where a new containment facility is commissioned or where a significant change in work practices is proposed;

e) Investigate incidents and accidents involving biological materials, in consultation with the BSC, and prepare incident reports for the BSC's review;

f) Liaise with the teaching hospital, the National Environment Agency, and other external bodies on matters relating to the transport, import, and export of biological materials;

